From ca3d938a24e89c38efd0906780c68167158cb04e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:41:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: use call_rcu_hurry() for EH host_failed update

scsi_eh_scmd_add() queues scsi_eh_inc_host_failed via call_rcu() to order the host state change before host_failed. With RCU lazy callbacks enabled, that callback could be delayed up to 10 seconds, delaying the SCSI/UFS error handler and recovery. Use call_rcu_hurry() to keep the existing bounded-time behavior.

Found by the r14 call_rcu audit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c b/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
index 3d3d13912..c02fadcaf 100644
--- a/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
@@ -276,7 +276,7 @@ void scsi_eh_scmd_add(struct scsi_cmnd *scmd)
 	 * Ensure that all tasks observe the host state change before the
 	 * host_failed change.
 	 */
-	call_rcu(&scmd->rcu, scsi_eh_inc_host_failed);
+	call_rcu_hurry(&scmd->rcu, scsi_eh_inc_host_failed);
 }
 
